 "This subtopic teaches students to communicate vision before production pressure starts."}, {"id": "005e693a-e922-4ad4-85de-33b3be9ad04d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "World-building and rules", "children": [{"id": "28a2cfe5-9bbd-439c-b39b-383335febba0", "type": "concept", "title": "Social world"}, {"id": "a51c7568-3d08-4e98-a4cd-747b39a49e5d", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual logic"}, {"id": "965b4cae-010f-4df6-8500-be1e659b56b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Sound world"}, {"id": "6c9a102e-cb33-41d7-8ce8-73124a7b51d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Behavioral rules"}], "description": "Directors define the rules of the world so actors, designers, and editors can make aligned choices."}]}, {"id": "8010e95d-8aa7-47dd-acc4-11e6dcba080b", "type": "topic", "title": "Visual Storytelling, Shot Design, Composition, and Camera Strategy", "description": "This section turns directorial intention into images through shot size, angle, movement, composition, lens choice, and visual progression.", "children": [{"id": "fcf584b2-ebf7-498f-953e-6f8ae3ed3174", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shot grammar", "children": [{"id": "8144aa22-e8b6-4664-8af8-d7bc77e8cd59", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot size"}, {"id": "92f0c245-d260-4bfa-a572-2c923fe42ec2", "type": "concept", "title": "Angle"}, {"id": "444c008d-2a5c-4b78-a5ef-9b66f34cbfac", "type": "concept", "title": "Lens perspective"}, {"id": "bbc34d75-dabd-471c-8d41-ea4bee512727", "type": "concept", "title": "Point of view"}], "description": "Students learn how camera placement and shot scale communicate power, proximity, isolation, and attention."}, {"id": "d346c538-0848-4fe1-ac61-a8855627ccfb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Storyboards, floor plans, and shot lists", "children": [{"id": "d4b4d2a6-c19b-4110-ae54-1bff33c0195e", "type": "concept", "title": "Overheads"}, {"id": "6dbc57b9-c9c1-41c8-bcd2-89cf44039e8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Storyboard panels"}, {"id": "163f96f3-b82a-4c69-ba04-22f3a463b33b", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot list priorities"}, {"id": "65f44541-f44d-4b14-854f-38a49ccdc37b", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage maps"}], "description": "Planning tools are treated as thinking tools rather than paperwork."}, {"id": "23b11c49-24cc-480c-aa4e-8e1cd5e0f8ed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual progression", "children": [{"id": "efb5ec8e-797f-43c0-bdf2-37bd7b646d11", "type": "concept", "title": "Escalation"}, {"id": "963b9439-eb3f-4b78-b686-84f3ec4ba03d", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast"}, {"id": "c7afac88-b756-480d-b87a-390867f3c74b", "type": "concept", "title": "Repetition"}, {"id": "5ba34312-90d1-4c6b-b147-3a7ffe058e66", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual payoff"}], "description": "Students design how image patterns change across a scene or film."}]}, {"id": "172402e2-f79c-4dd7-8005-f65adf64bd1e", "type": "topic", "title": "Blocking, Staging, Movement, Space, and Screen Geography", "description": "Blocking is where story, character, camera, space, and rhythm meet in physical action.", "children": [{"id": "74c5104f-3769-48f3-8fec-1e4fdc99e4a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Blocking for intention", "children": [{"id": "0c0c793d-bd31-48df-bfe8-6d096bd768f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Entrances and exits"}, {"id": "d9d6d352-de76-45ad-8102-1b3bb22f51c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Status shifts"}, {"id": "33a4af9e-accf-49ca-8f07-d70e941d3e01", "type": "concept", "title": "Proximity"}, {"id": "c454d2aa-87a3-4715-871d-7031950c1c9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Reveals"}], "description": "Students connect actor movement to objectives, relationships, and scene turns."}, {"id": "138306e5-2274-43eb-8358-d4ea1887bd19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Staging for camera and stage", "children": [{"id": "95fde976-61dc-429d-8a4e-b7319e927d62", "type": "concept", "title": "Sightlines"}, {"id": "02412845-ba51-4a42-a216-58408fe0ef4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Depth"}, {"id": "a7ff9b8e-8dd2-4f3b-bd9a-13848485ea07", "type": "concept", "title": "Axis of action"}, {"id": "b4e37f0b-8bf9-4b8e-b0f5-ae9b3697012d", "type": "concept", "title": "Planes of space"}], "description": "The course compares cinematic framing with theatrical composition so students can direct across media."}, {"id": "ab38e1e8-5577-4620-8252-94382a7ad609", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuity and geography", "children": [{"id": "af6a9109-fbee-4960-b0be-b85b3c659f08", "type": "concept", "title": "180-degree rule"}, {"id": "068ad748-0c83-4bcb-b345-5e0d0ba65e3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Eyelines"}, {"id": "4acb31a9-0f15-4c9e-9782-0cceb152a141", "type": "concept", "title": "Screen direction"}, {"id": "36f61025-77aa-4dbc-85de-8b89199f4bdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Spatial transitions"}], "description": "Students learn to preserve clarity while using movement and coverage creatively."}]}, {"id": "9f23125c-6cc2-4cc9-b4c3-dc49310ccd4f", "type": "topic", "title": "Working with Actors, Casting, Rehearsal, and Performance Direction", "description": "Effective directing requires playable communication with actors, not vague result-oriented notes.", "children": [{"id": "cc971c4d-edc0-4593-bd56-1bb1e221b2ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Casting and actor fit", "children": [{"id": "00fafc34-6a68-4366-8157-d922092a02d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Auditions"}, {"id": "0e24c069-4bfb-48af-b96e-ac72013bcdae", "type": "concept", "title": "Callbacks"}, {"id": "c71d946b-4a58-46ca-82f4-c797faf5b2dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Chemistry reads"}, {"id": "da6d0e62-fc6e-4b84-958e-48735e686681", "type": "concept", "title": "Inclusive casting"}], "description": "Students learn how casting shapes interpretation, chemistry, rhythm, and production feasibility."}, {"id": "29fb0576-65b7-4eab-b2f0-c63ef7a2154b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Playable direction", "children": [{"id": "0f9d0f15-37ba-41a9-9cfe-1c52283d79b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Action verbs"}, {"id": "12451d16-3e06-48f8-abb3-2f67becf20c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Given circumstances"}, {"id": "912980b